    board(qa): file CF-185 — the shipped lane loader has no read-only mode and no overridable write target. Addresses CF-185.
    
    QA lane code-factory-duckbrain-qa-2026-11-04-09-00-46 re-verified six complete rows at
    origin/main 171bf23 (CF-155 probe rc 0 with 36 sections matching the plan; CF-153 ref
    forwarding arm PASS with the payload carrying --ref 'master' and its quoted twin; CF-156
    secret-scanning open=0 and alert 1 resolved used_in_tests with the named comment; CF-157
    census recipe 19 rows / one disabled, README no longer asserts the enabled state; CF-159
    injection probe INJECTION_EXECUTED=no and all remote-command sites shq-quoted; CF-176
    enabled sentence gone and the one-query census prints ratio+flag side by side; whole suite
    SELFTEST: PASS, 121 PASS / 19 intentional FAIL rows).
    
    Three classes that reproduced are NOT re-filed: the unresolvable 64-hex tree_fp on every
    complete row's evidence entry is CF-144, node.json bus.base from an unset CRIER_BASE is
    CF-078, and the ${HERE}/ spelling gap in the staged-set validator is CF-087.
    
    CF-185 is new: scripts/add_family_lanes.py reads argv nowhere (argv_handling=0), its write
    targets are literals (API = http://127.0.0.1:9090, DB = ~/.hermes/.../scheduler.db) so the
    hazard cannot be contained in a fixture, and it harvests the operator token from
    /proc/<MainPID>/environ at import — on a host without that PID it dies with
    FileNotFoundError, on this host it would PUT the live scheduler from --help.
    
    Guard bypass (disclosed): board-only diff, Tier 1 DEGRADED PASS by design (CF-031) — the
    lint scope is bash -n over staged *.sh and no implementation file is staged. tests/selftest.sh
    and scripts/boardctl validate were both run on this tree before the commit.
